 "brief": "Circuit: Repeater delay line (12 game ticks). Input: lever A at [-1, 1, 0] on the stone block [0, 1, 0]. Output: note block Q at [4, 1, 0]; Q is on while the note block is powered. The lever, its block and Q belong to the harness: do not move, replace or build on them. This build meets the spec in vanilla 26.3, but here the physics is changed: repeater_unit = 3 (game ticks per repeater delay step (vanilla 2, so delays 1-4 are 2/4/6/8 gt)). The spec is fixed in game ticks. Modify the build so that Q matches the spec under the changed physics. Your build is checked by toggling the lever on the spec's schedule and comparing Q's on/off edges, tick by tick, with the spec. Stay inside the bounding box and the block budget; allowed blocks are the benchmark allow-list. ",
